<font color=white><A HREF="/index.pl?node_id=2479&lastnode_id=175">Farewell, for now</a> (1 Replies)</font></td>
<td align=right bgcolor=#333333>
<nowrap><font color=white>Posted by <A HREF="/index.pl?node_id=2436&lastnode_id=175">Dalamoor</a> on 2001-10-23 20:56:57</font></nowrap></td></tr>
<tr><td colspan=2>It is with a heavy heart that I must bid you all farewell for now.  A good friend of mine needs help in strengthening his newly created Guild. He has asked me for my help, and as his friend I will.  I shall be gone only as long as it takes, then I will return.  I will show them the ways I have leaned from the Horde. If there is anything I can do to help, please let me know. May you all bathe in pools of everflowing blood.  <br>
Aluve my friends, <br>
Dalamarr Nightsun 31st Season Necromancer<br>
"COMBAT ENGINEERS LEAD THE WAY"</td></tr><tr><td colspan=2>&nbsp;</td></tr><tr><td bgcolor=#333333>
<font color=white><A HREF="/index.pl?node_id=2478&lastnode_id=175">SPECIAL Blood Fist and Bone Crush Guild Meeting!!!!</a> (0 Replies)</font></td>
<td align=right bgcolor=#333333>
<nowrap><font color=white>Posted by <A HREF="/index.pl?node_id=781&lastnode_id=175">Inertia</a> on 2001-10-23 15:32:45</font></nowrap></td></tr>
<tr><td colspan=2>There will be a special Guild Meeting for Blood Fist and Bone Crush members ONLY this Friday at 9PM EST (figure it out for your time zone....YOU LIVE THERE) at the Neriak Arena area.<br>
<br>
As stated before, this meeting is ONLY for those in the Bone Crush and Blood Fist battalions. In other words....if you are above level 46...go somewhere else >8P<br>
<br>
Please try your best to attend, and if you are KOS in Neriak (FIE ON YOU!!) then please try and be near the Nektulos Zone, as the meeting WILL involve some group strategies that will be demonstrated at the meeting, and we can come to you after the speech part of the meeting is done.<br>
<br>
Hope to see you all there, and may you Bleed Well.<br>
<br>
Inertia Dampers<br>
Warmistress<br>
One of the CONSTANT<br>
You will know us by the trail of the DEAD</td></tr><tr><td colspan=2>&nbsp;</td></tr><tr><td bgcolor=#333333>
<font color=white><A HREF="/index.pl?node_id=2472&lastnode_id=175">Thank you, Horde!</a> (2 Replies)</font></td>
<td align=right bgcolor=#333333>
<nowrap><font color=white>Posted by <A HREF="/index.pl?node_id=1313&lastnode_id=175">Kartane</a> on 2001-10-23 07:40:45</font></nowrap></td></tr>
<tr><td colspan=2>My family, <br>
<br>
My blood has turned to bile.  The hatred of my choice is now a branding on my soul.  And the blade in my hand is an extension of my Lord Innoruuk’s twisting taint upon this world.  The Blood Bringer has found her Rage…<br>
<br>
There are those who might take lightly this accomplishment.  But for those who kept me company as I carefully stole from the pockets of guildmasters, for those who brought me along to kill one very annoying fish man, for those who where there when my first chance was dashed and all my work to that point was lost… you know how much this means to me and that this was not as easy or fast road to travel.  I worked very hard for this moment of pure bliss.  And in this moment, you are the people that I wish to thank.     <br>
<br>
I want to thank everyone in the guild for their support and their presence… or for simply being a member of the family I am so proud to be a part of.  Inertia, my Warmistress, your support and understanding has always been unwavering and invaluable.  And Rekka, I am still thanking you for taking on the responsibility of organizing raids and Renux fights… and for literally giving me the robe off of your back.  Thank you Pustule, for spending your time trying to catch that Kedge and being our basic means of transportation so often.  I still owe you one uber (Ack! Forbidden word!) gift.  Thanks Gnormagn, for the rez when Tani caught me in the act of dipping into his pockets and for always being there whenever you could.  And Deftnoes… thank you for being the best taunter a rogue could ever ask for, for not giving up, and for not letting me give up either.    <br>
<br>
And it was not just with the Horde that I found such friends.  I’d like to thank all of Scarlet Underground.  Thank you Kitzu, for encouraging me when I needed it and for leading a young rogue, inexperienced on the planes, through Hate and to her book.  Thanks to Bearwolf, for being constantly helpful, funny, and so damn good at what she does that I keep forgetting that she’s actually a stinky druid.  And thank you Sirik, for just being the person you are… the sort of person who makes me proud to call Scarlet Underground an ally.<br>
<br>
Of course, many thanks to Kloth… for the robe and for his willingness to help a Hordling.  Mr. Silent Death, it was watching people like you that made me want to strive to be the Hordling I am today.  Having you with me in this endeavor was an honor.  Your name may no longer proclaim you Horde, but you’ll always feel like Horde to me.<br>
<br>
And a huge thanks goes out to all of Shadow Council, for remembering a rogue and giving her a first and second chance.  A special thanks of course is reserved for the gnomes of Shadow Council.  Glicknib, Moneaone, and Dogge… for coming at a moments notice when I needed you, and for thinking of me when you needed a rogue.  Congrats again Dogge on your snake stick.  Glad to think that some locks I picked helped you in some way to get it.  And many thanks to Glicknib, for never forgetting me and for proving to me yet again that Gnomes may be horrible, bald, leg humping, freaks of nature… but they make terribly valuable and endearing cohorts.<br>
<br>
The words of encouragement from all of you kept me going even after I was forced to begin it all again.  And with this, we can only believe that in our future battles, our foes shall fall faster.  Though this dagger in my hand is of a god-shaming beauty and shows me a power I could only imagine before… it would mean nothing if I did not wield it in the service of the Horde.  This entire game of our existence would mean nothing without all of you.  I look forward to being able to repay each and everyone of you for the time and service you have rendered me.  I look forward to seeing such items of power in your hands.  <br>
<br>
May my blade serve the Horde until the day my blade moves no more.<br>
<br>
K<br>
<I>Blood Bringer<br>
Devotee of Saryrn<br>
Black Venom Battalion</I><br>
</td></tr><tr><td colspan=2>&nbsp;</td></tr><tr><td bgcolor=#333333>
